  "facts": [
    "The current Sousa Bridge opened its southern span on December 9, 1939, and the northern span followed a year later, completing a continuous steel plate girder structure that replaced an iron girder bridge built in 1890.",
    "Named after the famed Marine Band conductor John Philip Sousa, the bridge honors a composer who grew up just a stone's throw from its northwestern terminus, linking history with modern infrastructure.",
    "The bridge’s construction was part of a long‑running political saga, with the 1950s Inner Loop Expressway debate leaving the northern approaches partially deconstructed until the District decommissioned the unfinished I‑695 segment in 2010."
